<BaseLayout title="Body and paint">
  <h1>Body and paint</h1>
  <p>The owner reference car is finished in Denim Blue; this page applies to the broader 2021 S60 range. Exterior trim, bumpers, grille, lighting, wheels, and sensor equipment vary by trim and package. The visible color name is useful for identification, but it is not enough to order an exact repair product: confirm the paint code on the vehicle before buying touch-up paint or arranging refinishing.</p>

  <ReferencePhoto src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c7/2019_Volvo_S60_T5%2C_rear_1.26.20.jpg" alt="Rear three-quarter view of a 2019 third-generation Volvo S60 T5" caption="Rear exterior reference for the third-generation S60; trim and bumper details vary by specification." credit="Kevauto" source="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2019_Volvo_S60_T5,_rear_1.26.20.jpg" license="CC BY-SA 4.0" />
  <h2>Paint identification</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Locate the vehicle identification and paint information label using the owner's manual.</li>
    <li>Record the paint code exactly as printed, including any suffix or variant.</li>
    <li>Give the code and vehicle details to the paint supplier; do not rely on a web listing that matches only the color name.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Washing and routine care</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Rinse loose grit away before wiping painted surfaces.</li>
    <li>Use clean, paint-safe wash media and separate materials for wheels and bodywork.</li>
    <li>Dry with a clean microfiber towel to reduce water spotting.</li>
    <li>Do not use household solvents or abrasive pads on painted trim.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Assessing a scratch</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Wash and dry the panel so dirt and transferred material do not disguise the damage.</li>
    <li>Check whether the mark is removable contamination or paint transfer using a paint-safe cleaner.</li>
    <li>Inspect under bright, indirect light. A scratch that catches a fingernail may extend below the clear coat; polishing cannot safely be assumed to remove it.</li>
    <li>If primer or bare metal is visible, arrange a suitable repair rather than leaving the area exposed.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>For a fingernail-catching scratch on a metal panel, avoid aggressive sanding or repeated machine polishing. Determine the damage depth first; a paint professional can assess whether localized touch-up or refinishing is appropriate.</p>

  <h2>Configuration differences</h2>
  <p>Momentum, R-Design, Inscription, and Polestar Engineered models can have different bumper styling, grille details, exterior trim, wheels, and lighting equipment. Parking sensors, cameras, and headlamp functions depend on installed options. Verify the exact part by VIN and compare connector and mounting details before replacing a component.</p>

  <h2>Exterior reference topics</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Lighting assemblies and bulb/service access.</li>
    <li>Mirrors, cameras, and parking sensors.</li>
    <li>Door, hood, and trunk operation.</li>
    <li>Wiper blades and washer system.</li>
    <li>Jacking points and underbody covers.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Vehicle identification labels</h2>
  <p>Use the paint code printed on the vehicle's own identification/product label, including any secondary color code. Volvo's <a href="https://www.volvocars.com/en-ca/support/car/s60/20w17/article/b0804d54c7fc096bc0a81f6f065ad63e_f512e0397febd1b3c0a801514a72cbd0/">2021 S60 type-designations guide</a> describes the identification labels and notes that U.S. and Canadian label placement differs. The label fitted to the car takes precedence over a generic illustration or trim name.</p>
